<!--Render Target Documentation — SetRendering
  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation.SetRendering-->
<rdoc:SetRendering xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:rdoc="com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    Set processor: STEPS and total, print, step, instance views
  </is>
  <documentation>
    A block whose baseType chain includes com.machineblocks.bml.core.Set is
    rendered by ScadSetProcessor as a SCAD set file. The file follows
    FileStructure. The placement array is the generated local gen_STEPS, a
    file-scope array in the customizer section /* [Hidden] */. The prefix is
    the generated-local prefix from FqnNaming. The main module takes config
    and settings and dispatches
    on mode. Total, Print, and Step each wrap their children in mb_block.

    A MachineBlocks set uses _parts, inherited from CompositeBlock, and _steps,
    declared on Set. Preset catalogs are BlockPresets(T), not an aggregation
    on Set.

    - _parts — placed instances (direction, offset; id becomes the SCAD
      instance id)
    - _steps — assembly order; optional; default is _parts document order.
      Repeating an id emits that same placement again. One instance module is
      emitted per distinct id. Its part type is the first placement with that id.

    gen_STEPS is generated from the placement list. Each entry:

        [instanceId, boundingBox, direction, offset]

    - [0] instanceId — string from the placed instance id
    - [1] boundingBox — [x, y, z] from the instance size, otherwise the placed
      type's size property default. A literal is copied. A constant expression
      is evaluated from that part's property values; a placement value overrides
      the type default of the same name. Preset merge is not applied. An
      expression that still depends on a runtime value counts as missing.
    - [2] direction — "west" | "north" | "east" | "south"
    - [3] offset — [x, y, z]

    Example:

        gen_STEPS = [
            ["00001", [16, 16, 1], "west", [0, 0, 0]],
            ["00002", [4, 4, 9], "west", [0, 0, 1]]
        ];

    The set bounding box is computed at SCAD render time by mb_parts_total_size.
    Total, Print, and Step pass it as the wrapper size:

        ["id", gen_blockId],
        ["base", false],
        ["studs", false],
        ["align", align],
        ["offset", offset],
        ["direction", direction],
        ["size", mb_parts_total_size(gen_STEPS)]

    id, align, offset, and direction of that wrapper are the set's own
    placement, read with mb_param_*. base and studs are false, so the wrapper
    draws no brick. Children render inside it. A parent can place the set.

    Four submodules, PascalCase suffixes, each (config, settings):

        ...DefaultEnclosure__Total
        ...DefaultEnclosure__Print
        ...DefaultEnclosure__Step
        ...DefaultEnclosure__Instance

    Total walks every gen_STEPS row and calls __Instance with settings taken from
    that row: id via mb_block_id(gen_blockId, instanceId), instanceId, size,
    direction, offset, baseColor, and assembly "merged".

    Print walks every row the same way. offset is
    mb_set_step_print_position(assembly, gen_STEPS, gen_i). direction is omitted, so
    the part stays on its default direction. assembly is mb_param_assembly of
    the caller. Parts sit in a row along X. The gap comes from the previous
    row's size. Unassembled assembly doubles that gap when the size is taller
    than it is wide.

    Step reads step, combined, and highlightColor. The module default for
    combined is false. The generated main call passes combined true, so the
    customizer shows steps before the current one in baseColor and the current
    step in highlightColor. With combined false, only the current step is
    drawn, in baseColor. Position and direction come from gen_STEPS. assembly is
    "merged". The current step is drawn when step is an index of gen_STEPS.

    __Instance reads instanceId and dispatches with if / else if to
    ...__Instance_00001. Those modules are templates. They read id, size,
    direction, offset, baseColor, and assembly from the settings of that call
    and forward them to the part manifestation. config is forwarded unchanged.
    The part's mb_block applies offset and direction. The same template can
    be called from several gen_STEPS rows. Instance mode forwards the caller
    settings and does not copy a gen_STEPS row. A customizer instance view then
    uses the part defaults for size, direction, and offset unless the caller
    supplied them.

    When _steps is absent, gen_STEPS follows _parts document order. A missing
    direction defaults to "west". A missing offset defaults to [0, 0, 0].
    A missing id, a missing size, or a size expression that is not constant
    returns files: [] and diagnostic BML_SET_PART_INCOMPLETE.

    Customizer variables, then hidden gen_STEPS:

        mode           = "total"; // [total:Total, print:3D Print, step:Step, instance:Instance]
        step           = 0;       // [0:n]  n is the last gen_STEPS index, or 0 when empty
        instanceId     = first gen_STEPS id, or "00001" when gen_STEPS is empty
        baseColor      = string property, otherwise "#EAC645"
        highlightColor = string property, otherwise "#55AB68"
        assembly       = "merged"; // [unassembled:Unassembled, assembled:Assembled, merged:Merged]

    baseColor and highlightColor use the MachineBlocks color dropdown
    (Turquoise through Asbestos). The main call passes mode, step, instanceId,
    baseColor, highlightColor, assembly, and combined true. The main module
    reads mode with mb_param(config, settings, "mode", default="total").

  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="rdoc:Customizer" relation="ReadNext" />
  </references>
</rdoc:SetRendering>
